Secure Access Secure Edge (SASE)
    - Combines networking and security functions into a single cloud-native service to ensure secure and seamless access for end-users
    - Uses SDN
    Most similar alignments of SASE:
    - AWS -> VPC
    - Azure -> Azure Virtual WAN or Azure ExpressRoute
    - Google -> Google Cloud Interconnect or Coogle Cloud VPN

Security Service Edge (SSE)
    - Subset of SASE
    - Focuses on security services
    -  Delivered as a service to provide secure access to the Internet, cloud services, and private applications
    - Secure Web Gateways (SWG)
        Filters unwanted software and malware from user-initiated web and Internet traffic
    - Cloud Access Security Brokers (CASB)
        Border device between cloud service consumers and the providers to monitor activity and enfore their security policies
    - Zero Trust Network Access (ZTNA)
        No user device, inside or outside of the org's network, is trusted
        